    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Till is a major type of sediment deposited directly by moving or melting glaciers.",
        "Glacial till consists of unsorted, unstratified material ranging from clay to large boulders.",
        "Till deposits form various glacial landforms such as moraines and drumlins."
      ],
      "id": "o05d9u2"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Remember that Till is unsorted and unstratified because it is deposited directly by ice, not sorted by water.",
        "Competitive exams often ask to distinguish Till (direct glacial deposit) from Outwash (fluvio-glacial deposit sorted by meltwater)."
      ],
      "id": "6ln2ge4"
